  "body": "Found during #3694 (PR #3700).\n\n## What happens\n\n`assets/posts/mach4.cps` writes an mm feed with one decimal (`ff()`, near line 103). The G84 tap feed is pitch x rpm. A feed with two or more decimals loses its fraction. Example: a tap feed of 34.56 mm/min posts as `F34.6` (0.12 percent).\n\n## Why it is wrong\n\nThe control cuts the pitch F / S. A rounded F gives a wrong pitch with no warning.\n\n## Done means\n\n- The tap feed keeps three mm decimals (four in inch), or a pitch that the words cannot hold within 0.01 percent is refused by name (as `haas.cps` does after #3694).\n- A test pins the F word of the tap block for a feed with two decimals.\n\nRefs #3694, #3699.\n\n",
